{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing length of the trip and states that trip_record.actual_distance_km 'may NOT be cited for the threshold test'. The trace measures 29.98 km across 229 fixes, with a 10-second sample interval, no gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. The distance the rider was billed against is therefore 29.98 km and the excess over the 24.0 km booked optimal is 5.98 km, not the rounded 6.00 km the receipt line implies.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km"
    },
    {
      "text": "Both POL-RD-01 gates pass on the trace figures. Excess of 5.98 km is 24.92% of the 24.0 km optimal route, which exceeds the 20% establishment gate, and 5.98 km is far above the 0.8 km absolute gate. The deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own telemetry, recorded as 'established' by the derived block, and it is not de minimis.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-08"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct"
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is discharged. Trip identifier TRP-00111 is the same on the trip record, the trace and the fare breakdown; the trace's first fix at 2026-08-03T07:47:40+08:00 is exactly the recorded trip start on the trip record, and the trace's last fix at 08:25:40 is the recorded end. The burden therefore shifts to the driver, who must point to a specific artifact and a specific clause; a general assertion that a road was closed does not discharge it unless an advisory artifact is named to carry it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00111", "EV-GPS-00111", "EV-FARE-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver cannot fall back on a rider-requested detour. The only rider message on this trip is 'as long as i reach by 8.30'; it names no place and no road, and the driver's own message is a notification ('i come off at bukit panjang ok'), not a request for rider consent. Both chat messages carry waypoint_hint null, so the 200 m corroboration test cannot be run at all. POL-RD-04 says the clause is then unavailable and the case is decided on the remaining clauses.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-08"]
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-03 exonerates a deviation only where the advisory names a road or segment that the optimal route traverses. The optimal route for this trip was produced by the platform's routing engine from an LTA traffic snapshot taken at 07:44, thirty-four minutes after this closure advisory went live at 07:10, and it still returned 'BKE southbound then PIE westbound' with no diversion. That route estimate is the very baseline POL-RD-01 fixes for this trip, and it is not consistent with the closed segment lying on the corridor the rider was billed against. The advisory cannot be used to wipe out 5.98 km of extra distance without the judge resolving that inconsistency first.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00111", "EV-ADVIS-00111-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-03(c) also requires the actual route to leave the optimal corridor before the affected segment and rejoin it after. The trace-derived facts supplied for this trip report fix counts, distances and speeds, not corridor geometry: 229 fixes, minimum distance 0.0 m, mean 7038.8 m, maximum 15193.2 m, four distinct speeds up to 71.0 kph. Nothing in that derived data places the vehicle on the diversion or shows where it left and rejoined the corridor, so on the present record that limb rests on the driver's own counterparty statement and his own chat message alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00111", "EV-CHAT-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the closure does not excuse the distance, the remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, run against the booked optimal because no POL-RD-03 adjustment applies: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 24.0 + 0.28 x 30.0) x the 1.0 surge_multiplier recorded on the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee = 31.00. The refund is charged_total 37.74 less 31.00 = 6.74, rounded up to SGD 6.75. That is the same order as the rider's own account that this route is 'never more than $32'; it is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis and far below the 90% full-refund share.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00111", "EV-TRIP-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable"
    },
    {
      "text": "If the judge cannot resolve the tension between the advisory's intersects_route flag and the 07:44-snapshot optimal route that kept the PIE westbound, POL-RD-10(7) applies: the driver's exoneration and the rider's measurement then rest on admissible yet mutually contradictory matter of comparable strength, and the case must go to a human reviewer. Under POL-GEN-03 an escalation holds the disputed amount rather than leaving it as a standing charge, which is the outcome the rider seeks on a record that cannot settle the question.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00111-01", "EV-TRIP-00111", "EV-GPS-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-03"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on either profile can be turned against this claim on this trip. rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 1 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, nowhere near the four-or-more claims POL-RD-08 requires before a sub-30% excess needs corroboration beyond the trace, and this excess is 24.92% in any event. POL-GEN-01 confines both profiles to the tests that name their fields, so no other line on either artifact - the driver's lifetime prior_deviation_flags included - may ground any finding about TRP-00111.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00111"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-GEN-01"]
    }
  ]
}
